// A call's arguments, each of which may hold at most one level of call
// nesting.
//
// Counted by call depth, not by expression depth: `f(g(x) + 1)` and
// `f(a[g(x)])` are one level (a single call, wrapped in an operator that adds
// no call of its own) and are allowed; `f(g(h(x)))` is two (`g`'s own
// argument is itself a call) and is rejected. The argument that carries the
// excess depth is the one reported, by position, because a call spread over
// several lines should name the line that is wrong.

chk_flat_args(int id) {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < len(((import nl1)[id]))) {
    i = chk_flat_at(id, i);
  }
} return void;
